Z||000003||Standard||06-11-2000||10:04 PM||||Wow that looks fantastic!  I think i'm gonna paint my wheels black when I re-do them. what did you use?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||06-11-2000||10:48 PM||||The black is Krylon "Rust Tough" paint in High Gloss Black. Then coated with Duplicolor Clear Urethane Wheel Paint.<BR>The wheels took about 4 hours per wheel to complete. That includes stripping, sanding then polishing the entire wheel.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Klown||06-11-2000||11:14 PM||||That looks great!  I may be wrong but I'm guessing your car is lowered.  What kind of springs did you use and why did you choose 225's instead of the 245's you had mentioned in some earlier posts.||||reg||14
Z||000006||Oreif||06-11-2000||11:29 PM||||I used Eibach springs, KYB shocks and struts, KONI sway bars, and Urethane bushings. The car is lowered approx. 1.5". <BR> I went with the 225's because the 245's were too wide for a 7" wheel. I also wanted the lower sidewall (4.4" with 225, 5.1" with 245)||||reg||1
